# Case study demo — local branch only (do not push to remote)

Copy into `.env.local` when working on the paper / case-study demo:

```env
VITE_CASE_STUDY_DEMO=1
```

## Branch layout

| Branch | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `evolve` | Shared product work (fork, tooltip labels, etc.). **No** case-study overlays. |
| `case-study/local` | Paper demo: session content patches. **Keep local; do not push.** |

```bash
git checkout case-study/local   # demo work
git checkout evolve             # normal development
```

## What `VITE_CASE_STUDY_DEMO=1` changes

No session overlays ship with this tree. The flag does nothing until a local override is added under `src/caseStudy/overrides/` (those `ses_*.ts` files are gitignored).
